{"name":"Fair Green","hex":"#92af88","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fair","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Beautiful, of a pleasing appearance, with a pure and fresh quality.","Unblemished (figuratively or literally); clean and pure; innocent."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something which is fair (in various senses of the adjective).","A woman, a member of the ‘fair sex’; also as a collective singular, women."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fair"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Middleton, Norfolk","blocks":[{"text":"Middleton is a village and civil parish in the English county of Norfolk.\nIt covers an area of 5.02 mi2 (13.0 km2) and had a population of 1,516 in 621 households at the 2001 census, reducing to 1,450 at the 2011 Census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Saint_Mary%27s_Church_at_Middleton_-_geograph.org.uk_-_255406.jpg/330px-Saint_Mary%27s_Church_at_Middleton_-_geograph.org.uk_-_255406.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Middleton%2C_Norfolk"},{"title":"Mitcham Common","blocks":[{"text":"Mitcham Common is 182 hectares (460 acres) of common land situated in south London. It is predominantly in the London borough of Merton, with parts straddling the borders of Croydon and Sutton. It is designated a Site of Metropolitan Importance for Nature Conservation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Mitcham_Common_1.JPG/330px-Mitcham_Common_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mitcham_Common"},{"title":"Fair","blocks":[{"text":"A fair is gathering of people for a variety of entertainment or commercial activities. Fairs are typically temporary with scheduled times lasting from an afternoon to several weeks. Fairs showcase a wide range of goods, products, and services, and often include competitions, exhibitions, and educational activities. Fairs can be thematic, focusing on specific industries or interests."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/2008Overview1.JPG/330px-2008Overview1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fair"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Seven_Islands_Pond%2C_Mitcham_Common_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1219991.jpg/500px-Seven_Islands_Pond%2C_Mitcham_Common_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1219991.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Seven_Islands_Pond%2C_Mitcham_Common_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1219991.jpg/500px-Seven_Islands_Pond%2C_Mitcham_Common_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1219991.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Seven Islands Pond, on Mitcham Common","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeven_Islands_Pond%2C_Mitcham_Common_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1219991.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Fairgames.jpg/500px-Fairgames.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Fairgames.jpg/1280px-Fairgames.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Fairgames.jpg/500px-Fairgames.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A boy at the fish pond, the Rockton World's Fair, harvest festival, Canada, 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFairgames.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Goose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg/500px-Goose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Goose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg/500px-Goose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Roundabouts (also known as a carousel or merry-go-round) are traditional attractions, often seen at fairs.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGoose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/1590_Mostaert_Dorf